second artist, birth date for a different person, or second sport is evidence to retain it. Check each proposed deletion once more against all originals before producing the final short list.\nInput: {\"question\": \"When was the South Calgary electoral district created?\", \"slot_hint\": \"other\", \"all_original_sources\": {\"D1S1\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0427-6303c6197fbb:d00\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 132, \"text\": \"Calgary-South East Calgary-South East (previously styled Calgary South East) is a provincial electoral district in Calgary, Alberta.\"}, \"D1S2\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0427-6303c6197fbb:d00\", \"start\": 133, \"end\": 208, \"text\": \"It has existed twice, first from 1959 to 1963, and then re-created in 2010.\"}, \"D1S3\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0427-6303c6197fbb:d00\", \"start\": 209, \"end\": 299, \"text\": \"The district is mandated to return a single member to the Legislative Assembly of Alberta.\"}, \"D1S4\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0427-6303c6197fbb:d00\", \"start\": 300, \"end\": 412, \"text\": \"The current electoral district was created from a portion of Airdrie-Chestermere, Calgary-Hays and Calgary-Shaw.\"}, \"D1S5\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0427-6303c6197fbb:d00\", \"start\": 413, \"end\": 530, \"text\": \"It contains the neighbourhoods of Auburn Bay, Chaparral, Copperfield, Cranston, Mahogany, New Brighton and Silverado.\"}, \"D1S6\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0427-6303c6197fbb:d00\", \"start\": 531, \"end\": 687, \"text\": \"The first provincial electoral district to use the name Calgary South East was created in the 1959 redistribution that saw the provincial ridings of Calgary\"}, \"D2S1\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0427-6303c6197fbb:d01\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 117, \"text\": \"South Calgary (provincial electoral district) South Calgary was a provincial electoral district from Alberta, Canada.\"}, \"D2S2\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0427-6303c6197fbb:d01\", \"start\": 118, \"end\": 223, \"text\": \"The electoral district returned a single member to the Legislative Assembly of Alberta from 1913 to 1921.\"}, \"D2S3\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0427-6303c6197fbb:d01\", \"start\": 224, \"end\": 306, \"text\": \"After 1921 the district was abolished and reconstituted to a five-member district.\"}, \"D2S4\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0427-6303c6197fbb:d01\", \"start\": 307, \"end\": 441, \"text\": \"The South Calgary electoral district was created in 1913 when the Calgary provincial electoral district was carved into three ridings.\"}, \"D2S5\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0427-6303c6197fbb:d01\", \"start\": 442, \"end\": 511, \"text\": \"The first election in 1913 featured a two candidate fight between Dr.\"}, \"D2S6\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0427-6303c6197fbb:d01\", \"start\": 512, \"end\": 597, \"text\": \"Thomas Blow Conservative candidate and well known Calgary area lawyer Clifford Jones.\"}, \"D2S7\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0427-6303c6197fbb:d01\", \"start\": 598, \"end\": 660, \"text\": \"Blow won the district with 71% of the popular vote, riding the\"}, \"D3S1\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0427-6303c6197fbb:d02\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 162, \"text\": \"Calgary Southeast Calgary Southeast was a federal electoral district in Alberta, Canada, that was represented in the House of Commons of Canada from 1988 to 2015.\"}, \"D3S2\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0427-6303c6197fbb:d02\", \"start\": 163, \"end\": 225, \"text\": \"The district was in the southeast part of the City of Calgary.\"}, \"D3S3\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0427-6303c6197fbb:d02\", \"start\": 226, \"end\": 282, \"text\": \"It was bounded by the city limits to the south and east.\"}, \"D3S4\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0427-6303c6197fbb:d02\", \"start\": 283, \"end\": 381, \"text\": \"The electoral district was created in 1986 from Calgary East, Bow River and Calgary South ridings.\"}, \"D3S5\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0427-6303c6197fbb:d02\", \"start\": 382, \"end\": 459, \"text\": \"In 1996, parts were transferred from this electoral district to Calgary East.\"}, \"D3S6\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0427-6303c6197fbb:d02\", \"start\": 460, \"end\": 611, \"text\": \"This riding has elected the following Members of Parliament: \\\"Note: Conservative vote is compared to the total of Progressive Conservative and Canadian\"}}, \"original_cards\": [{\"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0427-6303c6197fbb:d00\", \"card_id\": \"ramdocs-0427-6303c6197fbb:d00:c0\", \"entity\": \"South Calgary electoral district\", \"scope\": \"provincial electoral district in Calgary, Alberta\", \"claim\": \"The first provincial electoral district to use the name Calgary South East was created in the 1959 redistribution.\", \"answer\": \"1959\", \"quote\": \"The first provincial electoral district to use the name Calgary South East was created in the 1959 redistribution that saw the provincial ridings of Calgary\", \"original_document_number\": 1}, {\"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0427-6303c6197fbb:d01\", \"card_id\": \"ramdocs-0427-6303c6197fbb:d01:c0\", \"entity\": \"South Calgary electoral district\", \"scope\": \"Creation date\", \"claim\": \"The South Calgary electoral district was created in 1913 when the Calgary provincial electoral district was carved into three ridings.\", \"answer\": \"1913\", \"quote\": \"The South Calgary electoral district was created in 1913 when the Calgary provincial electoral district was carved into three ridings.\", \"original_document_number\": 2}, {\"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0427-6303c6197fbb:d02\", \"card_id\": \"ramdocs-0427-6303c6197fbb:d02:c0\", \"entity\": \"South Calgary electoral district\",